{"ts":"2026-08-13T14:30:33.429Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6832c7c82d2c8091d5eebb8f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.231","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-13T14:30:33.429Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Re-measured 2026-08-13 with a wider denominator, which changes the size of the problem rather than confirming it.\n\nCounting top-level commands, the placeholder census is now 29 of 72 rather than 32 of 76, so the ratio is roughly unchanged while the surface shrank by four.\n\nCounting declared command paths — the unit an agent actually resolves — the picture is different. contracts --json --full declares 159 paths: 81 top-level and 78 subcommand. It emits 72 summaries, six of which name extension command groups that appear in no path list, so 66 declared paths carry a summary and 93 carry none. Every subcommand path is in the uncovered set. Combining both effects, a path that states a real intent exists for 43 of 159, or 27 percent.\n\nThe consequence for this item's scope: closing it by filling in 29 placeholder strings would leave 93 paths with no row to hold an intent at all. Filed pm-pmrae8 for the coverage half, which also carries the sequencing risk that every consolidation under pm-n7rr moves a command from the covered half into the uncovered one."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T14:30:33.429Z"}],"before_hash":"b9ca9aa1f3565fd5f88a9fb44ad38b4c3eb3272f7a9b19fdad7228577cd629ad","after_hash":"b6f3617082a9766075ff59f541d9362a6b3527d6db9a8687ba5237f424e764d2","item_hash_version":2}
